{
    "background_story": "Belen was a skilled woodworker and furniture maker who lived in a small village nestled in the rolling hills of the countryside. She was particularly renowned for her exquisite craftsmanship of traditional wooden bridges, where the crosspiece was the crowning glory of her designs. Belen's attention to detail and dedication to her craft were evident in every carefully shaped and fitted piece of wood. Her most famous creation was a majestic wooden bridge that spanned the village's main river, its crosspiece adorned with intricate carvings that seemed to dance in the sunlight. The bridge became a beloved landmark, and Belen's reputation as a master woodworker spread far and wide. People would come from all over to marvel at her handiwork and learn from her expertise.",
